     rraaddiiuussccttll _c_o_m_m_a_n_d [_a_r_g_u_m_e_n_t _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rraaddiiuussccttll utility controls the radiusd(8) daemon.

     The following commands are available:

     tteesstt _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e _r_a_d_i_u_s___s_e_c_r_e_t _u_s_e_r___n_a_m_e [options]
             Sends a RADIUS authentication request packet and shows the re‐
             sult.  The request is for the user specified by _u_s_e_r___n_a_m_e and
             sent to the RADIUS server specified by _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e.  _r_a_d_i_u_s___s_e_c_r_e_t
             is the shared secret with the server.  The options are as fol‐
             lows:

             iinntteerrvvaall _s_e_c_o_n_d_s
                     Specifies how many seconds to wait before resending a
                     packet.  The default is 2.

             mmaaxxwwaaiitt _s_e_c_o_n_d_s
                     Specifies the maximum amount of time to wait for a valid
                     reply packet.  The default is 8.

             mmeetthhoodd _m_e_t_h_o_d
                     Use _m_e_t_h_o_d for authentication.  It can be either ppaapp,
                     cchhaapp, or mmsscchhaappvv22.  If this option is omitted, ppaapp is
                     used.

             nnaass--ppoorrtt _n_a_s_-_p_o_r_t
                     Specify an integer value for the NAS-Port attribute in
                     the packet.  If this option is omitted, 0 is used.

             ppaasssswwoorrdd _p_a_s_s_w_o_r_d
                     Use _p_a_s_s_w_o_r_d for _u_s_e_r___n_a_m_e.

             ppoorrtt _p_o_r_t
                     Use _p_o_r_t when sending a packet to _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e.  If the port
                     is omitted, the default port number 1812 is used.

             ttrriieess _n_u_m_b_e_r
                     Specifies the number of packets to try sending.  The de‐
                     fault is 3.

             mmssggaauutthh _y_e_s | _n_o
                     Specifies if Message-Authenticator is given for the ac‐
                     cess request packet.  The default is yes.

     iippccpp sshhooww
             Show all ipcp sessions in the database of radiusd_ipcp(8)
             briefly.

     iippccpp dduummpp [--jjssoonn]
             Dump all ipcp sessions in the database of radiusd_ipcp(8).  When
             --jjssoonn is specified, rraaddiiuussccttll shows the sessions in JSON format.

     iippccpp mmoonniittoorr [--jjssoonn]
             Monitor the database of radiusd_ipcp(8), show newly created ses‐
             sions and deleted sessions.  When --jjssoonn is specified, rraaddiiuussccttll
             shows the sessions in JSON format.

     iippccpp ddiissccoonnnneecctt _s_e_q_u_e_n_c_e
             Request to disconnect the session specified by the _s_e_q_u_e_n_c_e.

     iippccpp ddeelleettee _s_e_q_u_e_n_c_e
             Request to delete the session specified by the _s_e_q_u_e_n_c_e without
             requesting disconnection.

